  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business (SDVOSB) set-aside program recorded $774M in obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 92.3% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years, and the program delivered 2,435 awards so far this fiscal year. The average award size was $318K. Historical full-year obligations show larger totals: FY22 totaled $8B, FY23 totaled $9.1B, FY24 totaled $8.8B, FY25 totaled $8.7B, and FY26 totaled $10.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs drove most of the FY2027 to date activity with $717M in obligations. Other agencies with notable FY2027 to date obligations include the Department of Homeland Security with $29.5M and the General Services Administration with $5.9M. Construction-related industries dominate the FY2027 to date industry mix, led by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $208M and several trades and services including Temporary Help Services at $75.3M and Other Computer Related Services at $73.7M. The top vendors in FY2027 to date include CITADEL FEDERAL SOLUTIONS LLC at $27.6M and SEMPER TEK CMS JV LLC at $26.7M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are FY2027 to date obligations across agencies?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the largest share with $717M in FY2027 to date obligations. The Department of Homeland Security followed with $29.5M and the General Services Administration followed with $5.9M. The remaining listed agencies each reported $4M or less in obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors captured the most SDVOSB set-aside dollars in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction led industries with $208M in FY2027 to date obligations. Temporary Help Services and Other Computer Related Services each recorded significant totals at $75.3M and $73.7M respectively. CITADEL FEDERAL SOLUTIONS LLC and SEMPER TEK CMS JV LLC were the top vendors with $27.6M and $26.7M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government award through SDVOSB set-asides?",
      "a": "The federal government awarded $774M through SDVOSB set-asides in FY2027 to date. The program made 2,435 awards so far this fiscal year and the average award size was $318K. Full-year comparisons show prior totals of $8B in FY22, $9.1B in FY23, $8.8B in FY24, $8.7B in FY25, and $10.1B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies use SDVOSB set-asides the most?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs uses SDVOSB set-asides the most, with $717M in obligations in FY2027 to date. The Department of Homeland Security and the General Services Administration followed with $29.5M and $5.9M respectively."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest SDVOSB set-aside contractors?",
      "a": "CITADEL FEDERAL SOLUTIONS LLC and SEMPER TEK CMS JV LLC are the largest SDVOSB set-aside contractors in FY2027 to date, with $27.6M and $26.7M respectively. Other top vendors include VALIANT CONSTRUCTION LLC at $26.1M and DANIELS BUILDING CO INC at $23.4M."
